  "id": "EDU103",
  "title": "The Alert Has a Date Stamp",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A resident wants to understand an urgent shared warning, but a cropped screenshot hides its location and date. Restoring those fields and checking the issuing authority prevents an old warning from being treated as a current instruction.",
  "hook": "Is this warning for this place and this time?",
  "visible_action": "A warning card expands to expose location, timestamp, and issuer fields; a verified-source check sits beside it.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "An alert’s source, location, time, and updates determine its relevance.",
  "gate": "Use a fictional alert with no active emergency instructions; verify local official alert procedures. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
